Hi, 

I didn't run the code but it looks fine. The row sum =1 constraint is because we want the values of each row to be weights, so that the numerator of Moran's index is the dot product between a vector of values and a lag vector computing average values of the neighbourhood of each location.

spca sets the diagonal and row-standardises the matrix for you, so there will be no difference if you don't do it.

Cheers
Thibaut
